                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There is absolutely nothing wrong with platformers that make you want to smash something into your monitor or induce an incredible wish for self-torture.\nAs long as you're the only one to blame this is all fine.\n\nBut if you keep on dying because the controls are bad, then the game is not difficult or challenging or demanding, no sir, in that case the game is just simply bad.\n\nGive me Super Meat Boy or Electronic Super Joy and you will see me rage, scream, cry, swear ... but you will never hear me saying that this or that was the game's fault.\nIn case of Yury, most of my deaths were the game's fault simply because the controls are so bad (and keys aren't rebindable) that the required precision is barely achieveable.\n\nYou like performing precision jumps just to get drowned in lava because you slide off the edge?\nYou like having to use the \"z\" key to jump?\nYou like finally managing one passage just to be forced to jump down without knowing what's below you?\nThen Yury is the game for you.\nI know it's not the game for me.\n\nP.S. You might be able to change keys in Unity's launcher, but that's like saying \"you can rebind it in the ini file\".",
